usage: replay_checks.py [-h] --repo REPO --output OUTPUT
                        [--batch {primary,expanded,both}] [--timeout TIMEOUT]

Replay the recorded repository commands on a user-provided checkout. This
writes new logs only under --output. It does not overwrite the frozen audit. A
Git checkout/index is needed by the repository's census tools. Existing Lean
and Arb dependencies are not installed automatically. Numerical checks can be
expensive; --batch primary is the default.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --repo REPO
  --output OUTPUT
  --batch {primary,expanded,both}
  --timeout TIMEOUT
